  "payload": {
    "evidence_contract": "judge_question:1",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-161024",
      "sequence_position": 6,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14128542/assets/a44852c606e67842a58ad1a696253e6e211816f8243beec8b3eea97ef42055a2.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,\\sqrt{2}\\le u\\le 3,\\,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{9}\\le v\\le \\frac{4\\pi }{9}\\},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v).\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be the image of the top side of $Δ$ under the action of $T?$",
      "worked_solution": "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the top side.\n\nFor the top side, we have $v=\\frac{4\\pi }{9}$ and $\\sqrt{2}\\le u\\le 3.$ \n\nSubstituting $v=\\frac{4\\pi }{9}$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{9}),\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{9})),\\,\\sqrt{2}\\le u\\le 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a parametric equation of the line segment that makes an angle of $\\frac{4\\pi }{9}$ with the positive $x$-axis and whose endpoints lie on circles of radii $\\sqrt{2}$ and $3$ centered at $O,$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14128542/assets/8c5ef04b3fa4765bbad1bd7345fe5217feac73c21251b99426c17ed22ec3bbd1.png)",
